  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2024 dataset is already showing early scholarly reuse: it has been cited once in the literature and is linked to eight downstream reuse records in the DataCite graph. The record supports a clear role as a technical underpinning for work on superconductivity and SIESTA-based simulation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Density functional Bogoliubov-de Gennes theory for superconductors implemented in the SIESTA code documents a computational implementation that brings together Bogoliubov-de Gennes theory and density functional theory within the SIESTA framework. The abstract indicates that the work is intended to describe conventional and unconventional superconducting states, including inhomogeneous superconductors and heterostructures, which helps explain why the dataset is being reused in related superconductivity research.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The clearest impact signal is scholarly uptake. OpenAlex records one citation, and the citing work is a 2024 article in Physical Review B. The citation context points to continued use in the same technical area, with superconductivity, density functional theory, and SIESTA all reflected in the citing landscape.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Reuse evidence is broader than the citation count alone suggests. The DataCite graph shows eight downstream reuse links, including the dataset itself, the associated preprint and journal article, and several related software and article records. This pattern is consistent with a resource that serves as supporting infrastructure for a methodological publication and its related outputs.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The surrounding attention record is otherwise quiet: there are no documented online mentions in the available event-data source, and the available DataCite usage counters show no recorded views or downloads. That does not diminish the work\u2019s value; it simply means the strongest evidence at present comes from scholarly citation and structured reuse rather than broader public attention.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the record positions this dataset as an early but credible contributor to superconductivity and electronic-structure research, with its impact emerging through research reuse, linked associated articles, and a first citation from a closely related journal paper.</p>",
